course: dictionary
lesson: 8202
title: Retake: taking it again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can give you a clue. The prefix re- often means again, so retake means take again. «Exams like GCSEs and A levels open doors later, but people who do badly can retake them or find other routes.» Swap your meaning into the sentence: people can take the exam again, and that still makes sense.
explain: Retake can also mean a second try at a scene in a film. If an actor does not get a scene right, the director may ask for a retake. The words around the word tell you which meaning is right: a test, a scene, or a place.
explain: Armies can retake a place they have lost. «From 1096 European Christians fought the Crusades to control Jerusalem.» Later, «Muslim leaders such as Saladin fought back and retook it in 1187.» Retook is the past tense of retake: the city was taken back again.
fact: Retake is a verb and a noun: you retake a test, or you have a retake.
fact: The verb forms are retake, retakes, retook, retaken and retaking.
fact: The prefix re- often means again, so retake means take again.
fact: In many British schools, a retake of an exam is called a resit.
fact: «Retook» is the past tense: «Saladin retook the city in 1187» means he took it back again in 1187.
exercise: «Exams like GCSEs and A levels open doors later, but people who do badly can retake them.» What does retake mean here? | Pass it without any work | Lose the exam paper | *Take the exam again | Cancel the exam forever
exercise: «Saladin fought back and retook it in 1187.» What did Saladin retake? | A film scene | A school exam | *Jerusalem, a city
exercise: A film director asks for a retake of a scene. What is a retake here? | A scene that is cut out forever | *A second try at filming the scene | A new film with new actors | A short break for lunch
test: Ravi failed his spelling test, so he will retake it on Friday. What does retake mean? | To cancel the test | To write a new spelling list | To copy his friend's answers | *To take the test again
test: Put the right word in the gap: The army lost the castle, but in 1187 it ____ the castle. | retaking | retakes | retake | *retook
exam: Which sentence uses retake to mean capture a place again? | The director will take a photo of the class | *The army will retake the castle from the enemy | She will retake the bus to school | He will take a long nap after lunch
